   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Paint from a shader (Flux 2 Klein)\n\n**You need:** Flux 2 Klein 4B: `flux-2-klein-4b.safetensors` (diffusion_models), `qwen_3_4b.safetensors`\n(text_encoders), `flux2-vae.safetensors` (vae). Other names: pick them in the three loaders.\n\n**kubakub region prompt** says which regions are painted and what they become: the first-floor windows, as stained\nglass. Queue once, then **pick regions** on it lists what your regions hold (groups, floors) to choose from. Its\n`which regions` output feeds the same field of the **kubakub shader**, so the choice is made once. The shader draws\nstripes in those windows; its `images` go to **`material`** of the region sampler, so the model paints its stained\nglass along the stripes. Try another preset with **browse the presets**, move its sliders with **adjust**.\n\n- how much of the shader stays: `denoise` on kubakub region prompt (0.5 = most of it, 0.9 = the composition only)\n- another prompt for other regions: a second kubakub region prompt behind the first (plan -> plan)\n- which moment of the shader: `material_at` on the sampler (advanced)\n- the shader as a reference instead of the start: `reference = material` in `more` of kubakub region prompt (the way\n  Qwen Image follows it)\n- where the model may change more: connect the shader's `masks` (or another shader's) to `change`\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
